{
  "id": "27815_senjiru",
  "headword": "{煎|せん}じる",
  "reading": "せんじる",
  "romaji": "senjiru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to decoct; to boil down; to brew (herbs, tea)",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to decoct; to boil down; to brew (herbs, tea)",
      "explanation": "To extract the essence of herbs, medicinal plants, or tea leaves by simmering them in water. Associated with traditional herbal medicine and tea preparation."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "27815_senjiru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{薬草|やくそう}を{煎|せん}じて{飲|の}む。",
      "english": "I decoct medicinal herbs and drink them.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27815_senjiru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{祖母|そぼ}は{風邪|かぜ}のときに{薬|くすり}を{煎|せん}じてくれた。",
      "english": "My grandmother would brew medicine for me when I had a cold.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27815_senjiru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{漢方薬|かんぽうやく}は、{決|き}められた{時間|じかん}だけ{弱火|よわび}で{煎|せん}じることが{大切|たいせつ}だ。",
      "english": "It is important to decoct Chinese herbal medicine over low heat only for the prescribed time.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Refers to simmering herbs, medicinal plants, or tea in water to draw out their active components. Strongly associated with {漢方|かんぽう} (traditional Chinese herbal medicine).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {薬|くすり}を{煎|せん}じる: to decoct medicine\n- {薬草|やくそう}を{煎|せん}じる: to brew medicinal herbs\n- {煎|せん}じ{薬|ぐすり}: a decoction; herbal brew\n\nThe idiom {爪|つめ}の{垢|あか}を{煎|せん}じて{飲|の}む means to imitate an admirable person, wishing one had their good qualities.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {煮出|にだ}す: to extract by boiling — close in meaning, used more for tea and broth\n- {淹|い}れる: to brew (tea, coffee) — for ordinary steeping, not medicinal decoction",
